{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790564498243,"sessionID":"ses_f1a0af382ffeVbrAqtSyvu0KyA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_eqSEmYx16lB5FLXKFeuj0Bi9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md\n+# Source resolution\n+\n+## Controlling rules\n+\n+Per `01_selection_rules.md` (effective 2026-05-08), when files conflict about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field. The roster is baseline information, while newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict. Archived, future-wave, and optional-add-on files are planning context only; they do not override current first-wave rules.\n+\n+`04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md` is newer than both `02_site_roster.csv` and `03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv` and therefore controls conflicting storage statuses. It reports no newer changes for the other clinics.\n+\n+## Effective storage status by roster clinic\n+\n+| Clinic ID | Clinic | Effective storage status | Controlling source |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| N-101 | Maple Junction Clinic | certified | No newer change; roster and 2026-04-18 audit agree. |\n+| N-102 | Riverbend Health | certified after mitigation complete | 2026-05-06 update: logger installation verified 2026-05-05. |\n+| N-103 | Pine Ridge Outreach | certified | No newer change; roster and 2026-04-18 audit agree. |\n+| N-104 | Lakeside Family Care | suspended | 2026-05-06 update: compressor fault; earliest retest after 2026-06-15. |\n+| N-105 | Cedar Works Clinic | certified | No newer storage change; roster and 2026-04-18 audit agree. Clinic closure is a separate eligibility field. |\n+| N-106 | Hillcrest Annex | certified | 2026-05-06 update: recertification completed 2026-05-05. |\n+| N-107 | Old Mill Clinic | conditional pass pending | 2026-05-06 update: repair delayed; status remains pending. |\n+| S-201 | South Gate Clinic | certified | No newer change; roster and 2026-04-18 audit agree. |\n+\n+The archived two-clinic/lowest-transport guidance, later-wave requests, and optional add-ons do not override the current first-wave selection rules. Current rules require exactly three eligible North-region clinics and prioritize the donor anchor if eligible, then the lowest-cost other eligible clinics.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/clinic_screen.md\n+# First-wave clinic screening\n+\n+Requirements used: North region, open during 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14, accepted effective storage status (`certified` or `certified after mitigation complete`), full-window coordinator coverage, delivery by 2026-06-07, and total selected cost within the $20,000 budget. Per-clinic cost is setup plus required transport. Cost is shown when the clinic meets all non-cost eligibility conditions; otherwise it is not applicable (`—`).\n+\n+| Clinic ID / name | Effective storage status | Coordinator full-window availability | Transport delivery | Rollout cost if otherwise eligible | Eligible | Blocking reason if no |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| N-101 Maple Junction Clinic | certified | Yes — Iris Patel | 2026-06-06 (SwiftRoute) | $7,400 ($6,200 + $1,200) | yes | — |\n+| N-102 Riverbend Health | certified after mitigation complete | Yes — Omar Singh | 2026-06-07 (NorthLine) | $6,450 ($5,500 + $950) | yes | — |\n+| N-103 Pine Ridge Outreach | certified | No — Lena Torres has a 2026-06-12 blackout | 2026-06-05 (SwiftRoute) | — | no | Coordinator is not available for the full launch window. |\n+| N-104 Lakeside Family Care | suspended | Yes — Noah Brooks | 2026-06-06 (SwiftRoute) | — | no | Storage status is suspended; earliest retest is after the launch window. |\n+| N-105 Cedar Works Clinic | certified | Yes — Sima Cho | 2026-06-08 (NorthLine) | — | no | Clinic is closed for maintenance and delivery misses the 2026-06-07 cutoff. |\n+| N-106 Hillcrest Annex | certified | Yes — Mara Ives | 2026-06-07 (Valley Freight) | $4,950 ($4,100 + $850) | yes | — |\n+| N-107 Old Mill Clinic | conditional pass pending | Yes — Tao Nguyen | 2026-06-05 (SwiftRoute) | — | no | Storage status remains conditional pass pending; door-seal repair is delayed. |\n+| S-201 South Gate Clinic | certified | Yes — Dee Alvarez | 2026-06-05 (CityCourier) | — | no | Region is South; first-wave requirement is North. |\n+\n+## Budget and selected-cost calculation\n+\n+First-wave budget: **$20,000** for setup plus required transport.\n+\n+Exactly three clinics meet all requirements: Maple Junction, Riverbend, and Hillcrest. Their total is **$7,400 + $6,450 + $4,950 = $18,800**, within budget by **$1,200**.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/launch_recommendation.md\n+# First-wave launch recommendation\n+\n+Select these three North-region clinics for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 rollout:\n+\n+| Clinic | Carrier | Delivery by | Rollout cost |\n+| --- | --- | --- | ---: |\n+| Maple Junction Clinic (N-101) | SwiftRoute | 2026-06-06 | $7,400 |\n+| Riverbend Health (N-102) | NorthLine | 2026-06-07 | $6,450 |\n+| Hillcrest Annex (N-106) | Valley Freight | 2026-06-07 | $4,950 |\n+\n+**Total rollout cost: $18,800. Remaining first-wave budget: $1,200** (from $20,000).\n+\n+Maple Junction Clinic is the donor continuity anchor and remains eligible. Preserve donor continuity code **MJ-14** in the rollout record. Riverbend's logger mitigation is complete, and Hillcrest's recertification is complete; all three selected coordinators have full-window coverage and deliveries meet the cutoff.\n+\n+## Rejected clinics\n+\n+- Pine Ridge Outreach: coordinator blackout on June 12.\n+- Lakeside Family Care: storage certification is suspended through the launch window.\n+- Cedar Works Clinic: closed for maintenance and delivery is after the cutoff.\n+- Old Mill Clinic: storage remains conditional pass pending.\n+- South Gate Clinic: South region, outside this North-region wave.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md\nA tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/clinic_screen.md\nA tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/launch_recommendation.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+# Source resolution\n+\n+## Controlling rules\n+\n+Per `01_selection_rules.md` (effective 2026-05-08), when files conflict about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field. The roster is baseline information, while newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict. Archived, future-wave, and optional-add-on files are planning context only; they do not override current first-wave rules.\n+\n+`04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md` is newer than both `02_site_roster.csv` and `03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv` and therefore controls conflicting storage statuses. It reports no newer changes for the other clinics.\n+\n+## Effective storage status by roster clinic\n+\n+| Clinic ID | Clinic | Effective storage status | Controlling source |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| N-101 | Maple Junction Clinic | certified | No newer change; roster and 2026-04-18 audit agree. |\n+| N-102 | Riverbend Health | certified after mitigation complete | 2026-05-06 update: logger installation verified 2026-05-05. |\n+| N-103 | Pine Ridge Outreach | certified | No newer change; roster and 2026-04-18 audit agree. |\n+| N-104 | Lakeside Family Care | suspended | 2026-05-06 update: compressor fault; earliest retest after 2026-06-15. |\n+| N-105 | Cedar Works Clinic | certified | No newer storage change; roster and 2026-04-18 audit agree. Clinic closure is a separate eligibility field. |\n+| N-106 | Hillcrest Annex | certified | 2026-05-06 update: recertification completed 2026-05-05. |\n+| N-107 | Old Mill Clinic | conditional pass pending | 2026-05-06 update: repair delayed; status remains pending. |\n+| S-201 | South Gate Clinic | certified | No newer change; roster and 2026-04-18 audit agree. |\n+\n+The archived two-clinic/lowest-transport guidance, later-wave requests, and optional add-ons do not override the current first-wave selection rules. Current rules require exactly three eligible North-region clinics and prioritize the donor anchor if eligible, then the lowest-cost other eligible clinics.\n\nIndex: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/clinic_screen.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/clinic_screen.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/clinic_screen.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@\n+# First-wave clinic screening\n+\n+Requirements used: North region, open during 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14, accepted effective storage status (`certified` or `certified after mitigation complete`), full-window coordinator coverage, delivery by 2026-06-07, and total selected cost within the $20,000 budget. Per-clinic cost is setup plus required transport. Cost is shown when the clinic meets all non-cost eligibility conditions; otherwise it is not applicable (`—`).\n+\n+| Clinic ID / name | Effective storage status | Coordinator full-window availability | Transport delivery | Rollout cost if otherwise eligible | Eligible | Blocking reason if no |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| N-101 Maple Junction Clinic | certified | Yes — Iris Patel | 2026-06-06 (SwiftRoute) | $7,400 ($6,200 + $1,200) | yes | — |\n+| N-102 Riverbend Health | certified after mitigation complete | Yes — Omar Singh | 2026-06-07 (NorthLine) | $6,450 ($5,500 + $950) | yes | — |\n+| N-103 Pine Ridge Outreach | certified | No — Lena Torres has a 2026-06-12 blackout | 2026-06-05 (SwiftRoute) | — | no | Coordinator is not available for the full launch window. |\n+| N-104 Lakeside Family Care | suspended | Yes — Noah Brooks | 2026-06-06 (SwiftRoute) | — | no | Storage status is suspended; earliest retest is after the launch window. |\n+| N-105 Cedar Works Clinic | certified | Yes — Sima Cho | 2026-06-08 (NorthLine) | — | no | Clinic is closed for maintenance and delivery misses the 2026-06-07 cutoff. |\n+| N-106 Hillcrest Annex | certified | Yes — Mara Ives | 2026-06-07 (Valley Freight) | $4,950 ($4,100 + $850) | yes | — |\n+| N-107 Old Mill Clinic | conditional pass pending | Yes — Tao Nguyen | 2026-06-05 (SwiftRoute) | — | no | Storage status remains conditional pass pending; door-seal repair is delayed. |\n+| S-201 South Gate Clinic | certified | Yes — Dee Alvarez | 2026-06-05 (CityCourier) | — | no | Region is South; first-wave requirement is North. |\n+\n+## Budget and selected-cost calculation\n+\n+First-wave budget: **$20,000** for setup plus required transport.\n+\n+Exactly three clinics meet all requirements: Maple Junction, Riverbend, and Hillcrest. Their total is **$7,400 + $6,450 + $4,950 = $18,800**, within budget by **$1,200**.\n\nIndex: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/launch_recommendation.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/launch_recommendation.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/launch_recommendation.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\n+# First-wave launch recommendation\n+\n+Select these three North-region clinics for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 rollout:\n+\n+| Clinic | Carrier | Delivery by | Rollout cost |\n+| --- | --- | --- | ---: |\n+| Maple Junction Clinic (N-101) | SwiftRoute | 2026-06-06 | $7,400 |\n+| Riverbend Health (N-102) | NorthLine | 2026-06-07 | $6,450 |\n+| Hillcrest Annex (N-106) | Valley Freight | 2026-06-07 | $4,950 |\n+\n+**Total rollout cost: $18,800. Remaining first-wave budget: $1,200** (from $20,000).\n+\n+Maple Junction Clinic is the donor continuity anchor and remains eligible. Preserve donor continuity code **MJ-14** in the rollout record. Riverbend's logger mitigation is complete, and Hillcrest's recertification is complete; all three selected coordinators have full-window coverage and deliveries meet the cutoff.\n+\n+## Rejected clinics\n+\n+- Pine Ridge Outreach: coordinator blackout on June 12.\n+- Lakeside Family Care: storage certification is suspended through the launch window.\n+- Cedar Works Clinic: closed for maintenance and delivery is after the cutoff.\n+- Old Mill Clinic: storage remains conditional pass pending.\n+- South Gate Clinic: South region, outside this North-region wave.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md","relativePath":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/answer/source_resolution.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+# Source resolution\n+\n+## Controlling rules\n+\n+Per `01_selection_rules.md` (effective 2026-05-08), when files conflict about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field. The roster is baseline information, while newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict. Archived, future-wave, and optional-add-on files are planning context only; they do not override current first-wave rul